I added the minimum charge in `total` in `src/invoice.ts`. The unit tests pass, but the slow ledger test fails, and that failure comes from the new rule.

The change is a floor at 10,000 cents applied to the final total, after discount and tax:

```ts
const MINIMUM_CHARGE_CENTS = 10_000;

export function total(invoice: Invoice): number {
  return Math.max(subtotal(invoice) - discount(invoice) + tax(invoice), MINIMUM_CHARGE_CENTS);
}
```

I applied the floor to the total after tax, so an invoice whose pre-tax amount is under $100 but whose taxed total reaches $100 is not raised. `toJSON` reads `total`, so the API output follows the same rule. I chose 10,000 cents as a named constant to match the integer-cents convention. I did not touch the tests.

The slow test `test/slow/ledger.test.ts` expects `$46992.00`, which is the sum without the minimum. It now gets `$47592.00`. The $600.00 difference is consistent with 12 invoices each being raised by $50.00 to the $100.00 floor. The test's expected value predates the change, so you will need to update it along with the other tests.

